  <taskbody>
    <context>Once you have set up your vehicle maintenance system, you need to perform a series of tasks to ensure the vehicle is in top condition.</context>
    <steps>
      <step>
        <cmd>Inspect</cmd>
        <info>Inspect the vehicle's engine, tires, and fluid levels to ensure everything is functioning properly before starting the maintenance process.</info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Replace</cmd>
        <info>Replace old engine oil and filters, as well as worn-out brake pads, ensuring your vehicle's performance remains optimal.</info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Test</cmd>
        <info>Test the battery, lights, and electronic systems to confirm all components are in good working order, reducing the risk of failures.</info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Clean</cmd>
        <info>Clean the vehicle, both inside and out, to maintain its appearance and prevent wear and tear caused by dirt and grime accumulation.</info>
      </step>
    </steps>
  </taskbody>
</task>